From dd3d4cae6e5d084aecfc03fb3be15376ddd12292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:55:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(h1): real permission gate via a PreToolUse hook

The approval gate previously only observed tool_use after claude had already run
the tool, and headless claude could not act at all without blanket pre-allow.
This adds a real gate: a PreToolUse hook in the VM (vm-image/swarm-pretooluse.sh)
classifies every call with the same rules as risk.ts via a classifier bundle that
lib/harness/permission-hook.ts generates (esbuild) and the runtime writes into the
VM. 'allow' proceeds; 'deny' blocks with exit 2; 'ask' writes <id>.req and
blocks until <id>.ok/<id>.no appears. runner.ts passes --settings + --permission-mode
acceptEdits; the runtime mirrors approval verdicts into the VM via writeFile so
the hook unblocks, using a deterministic id (hookApprovalId) shared with the hook.
esbuild is a prod dependency; next.config externalizes it; the Dockerfiles install
the hook and copy esbuild into the standalone output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
